WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.300
Previously on The O.C.:

00:00:00.869 --> 00:00:03.163
- Previously on The Valley:
- Stay in Tarzana.

00:00:03.414 --> 00:00:04.999
Previously on The Valley:

00:00:05.249 --> 00:00:07.252
I don 't feel like I fit here in Tarzana.

00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:09.421
You owe it to yourself.
Get out. Get free.

00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:13.092
- Why do I need to leave? You're here.
- Exactly.

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:15.679
- Luke.
- Luke came by to defrag my hard drive.

00:00:15.846 --> 00:00:17.431
- You look so hot.
- Now, forgive me...

00:00:17.723 --> 00:00:20.852
...this can't possibly be happening, right?
I'm crazy.

00:00:21.102 --> 00:00:23.522
I have this whole life to figure out.
And so does Ryan.

00:00:23.731 --> 00:00:25.733
Take care of him.

00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:27.611
I'll see you.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.456
So then did you take your watch off
during the deed, or what exactly?

00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:40.001
Wanna wait in the car?
I can pick this up myself.

00:00:40.168 --> 00:00:42.004
No, I got more questions.
I don't understand...

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.006
...did you take it
off before foreplay?

00:00:44.173 --> 00:00:46.509
- That would seem presumptuous...
- No, seriously...

00:00:46.759 --> 00:00:50.180
I like to leave the watch on. I like
to leave it on to know how I'm doing...

00:00:50.431 --> 00:00:51.891
...if I'm beating my old time.

00:00:52.058 --> 00:00:54.603
It's sort of a sex marathon,
not a sex sprint.

00:00:54.769 --> 00:00:56.230
Excuse me. Hi.

00:00:56.438 --> 00:00:59.150
I called earlier about the watch
that was left here.

00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:01.236
Room 204, right?

00:01:01.486 --> 00:01:03.906
Yeah. Such a nice girl
was staying in there.

00:01:04.073 --> 00:01:06.910
Beautiful too. Your girlfriend?

00:01:08.912 --> 00:01:11.874
- Okay. That's a little awkward.
- No, she's not. But thank you.

00:01:12.083 --> 00:01:13.167
A girl like that?

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:16.213
- You'd be a lucky guy if you could...
- Thank you for your time.

00:01:16.505 --> 00:01:18.382
Or his time. The timepiece.
Thanks a lot.

00:01:21.636 --> 00:01:23.931
One day, we'll look back on that
and we'll laugh.

00:01:24.098 --> 00:01:26.392
We'll laugh, laugh some more,
have a good laugh.

00:01:26.559 --> 00:01:29.104
Not at my timepiece joke,
but at the situation.

00:01:29.271 --> 00:01:31.065
I'm fine.
Theresa's back with Eddie...

00:01:31.232 --> 00:01:33.526
...where she should be. Right?
- Yes. Absolutely.

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:36.780
This is a good time for Ryan Atwood.
This is "Clean-Slate Ryan."

00:01:36.947 --> 00:01:40.660
Finally, you have no women to protect
from violent, goateed factory workers...

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:43.080
...or pill-popping manic-depressives.
- You're right.

00:01:43.247 --> 00:01:45.374
- I really do have a clean slate.
- You do.

00:01:45.541 --> 00:01:47.585
Dude, since day one
of you getting here...

00:01:47.836 --> 00:01:49.963
...it's been nothing but lady drama
with you.

00:01:50.214 --> 00:01:53.134
Marissa, Theresa, Luke, Oliver, Eddie.

00:01:53.301 --> 00:01:56.388
- I'm exhausted just thinking about it.
- I am kind of tired.

00:01:56.555 --> 00:02:00.101
Should be. But you know what?
You're gonna get a break. You deserve it.

00:02:00.268 --> 00:02:02.271
Think I'm gonna declare this month...

00:02:02.437 --> 00:02:04.982
...Angst-Free Ryan Month.
- Think it'll last all month?

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:09.446
Angst-Free Ryan Week. With an option
for an additional week, if you like it.

00:02:10.114 --> 00:02:11.616
- Okay. Thanks, bud.
- Right on.

00:02:12.283 --> 00:02:14.870
Hey. What's Luke doing here?

00:02:15.036 --> 00:02:17.289
- Tell him about your watch?
- No. Why would I?

00:02:40.652 --> 00:02:42.154
It didn't even last the night.

00:03:33.218 --> 00:03:36.430
I can't believe they were at a motel.

00:03:36.597 --> 00:03:39.976
It's just... It's so cheap.
It's so tawdry.

00:03:40.143 --> 00:03:43.439
Yeah. That's the real moral
of the story here.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.609
You know we're gonna have to see
Luke at school today, right?

00:03:49.905 --> 00:03:51.616
How could he do it?

00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:55.245
I mean, I get how he could do it,
it's Mrs. Cooper, but...

00:03:55.454 --> 00:03:58.457
What about her?
It's her daughter's ex-boyfriend.

00:03:58.749 --> 00:04:01.044
- Lf Marissa found out...
- No. She cannot find out.

00:04:01.294 --> 00:04:03.756
- She doesn't handle bad news well.
- It's gotta end...

00:04:04.006 --> 00:04:06.467
...before she finds out.
- I agree.

00:04:07.594 --> 00:04:09.596
Maybe you should take the reins
on this one.

00:04:09.847 --> 00:04:12.767
I would, but I feel like
it's more your speed.

00:04:15.145 --> 00:04:17.189
Sandy, Jimmy's here.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:18.608
Hot, hot, hot. Hey.

00:04:18.774 --> 00:04:20.902
- How are you, Jimmy?
- We're screwed.

00:04:21.152 --> 00:04:24.031
Oh, good. Nothing like a little
optimism in the morning.

00:04:24.198 --> 00:04:26.326
I'm serious.
Opening day is around the corner.

00:04:26.576 --> 00:04:28.328
We've got no contractor, no designer.

00:04:28.578 --> 00:04:31.582
- When did you last look at the books?
- I don't. That's your job.

00:04:31.791 --> 00:04:36.588
Well, we've basically blown through
our entire budget.

00:04:38.257 --> 00:04:40.927
You're really not so good at
managing the money, are you?

00:04:41.094 --> 00:04:42.971
No. I'm really not.

00:04:47.185 --> 00:04:50.815
- How did that happen?
- Construction, labor, permits.

00:04:51.065 --> 00:04:52.525
Oh, wow.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.822
A letter from Hailey.

00:04:58.199 --> 00:05:01.077
She's an aerobics instructor at Club Med
in Turks and Caicos.

00:05:01.244 --> 00:05:03.080
Turks and Caicos? Wow.

00:05:03.247 --> 00:05:05.666
- Unbelievable.
- That is unbelievable.

00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:07.085
Hailey got a job.

00:05:07.252 --> 00:05:10.255
So I'm gonna spend the weekend
interviewing designers.

00:05:10.548 --> 00:05:12.133
Not that we can afford any of them.

00:05:12.383 --> 00:05:14.219
Julie's gonna take Marissa
so I can work.

00:05:14.386 --> 00:05:18.224
I better get to work so I can make
some more money that you and I can lose.

00:05:18.391 --> 00:05:21.686
So you want a designer on the cheap?
How cheap? Like, free?

00:05:21.978 --> 00:05:23.731
Free is cheap.

00:05:24.982 --> 00:05:26.401
Julie.

00:05:27.402 --> 00:05:29.571
No. No way.

00:05:30.322 --> 00:05:33.159
- She's good.
- Yeah. At manipulating others.

00:05:33.409 --> 00:05:34.870
And backstabbing, pot-stirring...

00:05:35.162 --> 00:05:37.540
...generally creating an atmosphere
of hate and distrust.

00:05:37.706 --> 00:05:39.626
Did a nice job on the
Newport Group offices.

00:05:39.876 --> 00:05:42.754
They were elegant and tasteful.
It was shocking, really.

00:05:43.005 --> 00:05:46.843
This restaurant is supposed to be
my oasis, my happy place.

00:05:47.051 --> 00:05:50.639
A place to rebuild after Julie.
Not a...

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:54.477
She's not doing to The Lighthouse
what she did to my marriage.

00:05:54.895 --> 00:05:59.192
Free is cheap, Jimmy.
I mean, what choice do we have?

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:03.322
You asked me, Coop, and I think it's best.
You need some time off.

00:06:03.572 --> 00:06:05.867
Ever since I've known you,
you've had a boyfriend.

00:06:06.075 --> 00:06:07.202
You're right.

00:06:07.369 --> 00:06:10.497
You need to be independent.
How else are you gonna find a new guy?

00:06:10.748 --> 00:06:13.334
You can't be with someone
until you can be by yourself.

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:15.337
- I can be by myself.
- And by "yourself"...

00:06:15.587 --> 00:06:18.466
...I mean still hanging out with me.
- Okay, good. Thank God.

00:06:18.633 --> 00:06:19.801
What's going on over here?

00:06:20.677 --> 00:06:22.638
- Can I have a hug?
- Grady had a late night.

00:06:23.597 --> 00:06:26.351
I don't know.
I guess they're filming something.

00:06:26.517 --> 00:06:30.648
- Oh, my God. Oh, my God, Coop!
- What? What?

00:06:30.898 --> 00:06:32.066
Grady Bridges.

00:06:32.233 --> 00:06:35.195
- Who's Grady Bridges?
- Jake Needleman, The Valley.

00:06:35.529 --> 00:06:39.242
- He is so cute.
- Really? You think?

00:06:39.492 --> 00:06:42.079
Yeah. Not in your traditional way,
but he's hilarious.

00:06:42.287 --> 00:06:46.209
He's so funny. I hear he,
like, improvises all of his scenes.

00:06:47.085 --> 00:06:49.963
Let's go say hi. Be cool, okay?

00:06:52.967 --> 00:06:56.680
Hey, Grady, we're your biggest fans.
The Valley is my favorite show.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.685
- Thank you. Cool. I'm glad you like it.
- I love it. Obsessed. Addicted.

00:07:00.936 --> 00:07:06.276
- So, what are you guys doing here?
- We are on what they call "location"...

00:07:06.401 --> 00:07:08.153
...which means we're
shooting a scene...

00:07:08.278 --> 00:07:11.282
My character starts dating
this girl from Newport.

00:07:11.532 --> 00:07:13.576
- No, you'll ruin it!
- Okay. Okay.

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:17.957
- Are you as obsessed as she is?
- Actually, I've never seen your show...

00:07:18.249 --> 00:07:19.250
- Coop!
- What?

00:07:21.169 --> 00:07:23.881
- See, now that's funny.
- Oh, that was funny.

00:07:24.131 --> 00:07:26.342
That was funny. Funny girl.

00:07:27.719 --> 00:07:29.054
Maybe they're not having sex.

00:07:29.304 --> 00:07:31.641
Maybe they just
spoon and watch Charlie Rose.

00:07:31.891 --> 00:07:33.852
You're right. That's probably it.

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:36.563
Oh, my God, you guys.
We have the craziest news ever.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:39.609
I mean, nothing you could tell us
could top this.

00:07:40.902 --> 00:07:42.905
We met Grady Bridges.

00:07:43.906 --> 00:07:46.326
Star of The Valley, the best show ever.

00:07:47.786 --> 00:07:50.915
Okay. Anyway, he invited us
to his birthday party tomorrow night.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.379
The star of a hit TV show invited you
to his cool Hollywood birthday party?

00:07:55.629 --> 00:07:58.090
- That is awesome.
- There's no need for jealousy.

00:07:58.341 --> 00:07:59.884
- I'd never date an actor.
- Really?

00:08:00.051 --> 00:08:01.052
Yes.

00:08:01.636 --> 00:08:04.515
- I got us a couple of plus-ones.
- Great.

00:08:04.765 --> 00:08:07.227
I have to show everybody
the pictures of me and Grady.

00:08:07.477 --> 00:08:08.937
Thank God I had my camera phone.

00:08:09.104 --> 00:08:11.107
They're the autograph of
the 21 st century.

00:08:11.315 --> 00:08:14.110
Summer, I'd like to see these photos.
Why don't we share.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.950
- So how's Theresa?
- She's good. She's back with Eddie.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.287
- Have you talked to her since she left?
- Yeah, we have...

00:08:22.538 --> 00:08:25.541
...but we're taking some time apart.

00:08:25.666 --> 00:08:27.836
- Best thing, I guess.
- Yeah.

00:08:31.966 --> 00:08:34.636
- Oh, we should go.
- Yeah.

00:08:36.972 --> 00:08:41.561
Good light. Exposed brick, it's a bit '80s,
but these trends are cyclical.

00:08:41.812 --> 00:08:44.815
South-facing windows.
These floors could be sanded.

00:08:44.982 --> 00:08:46.943
And the beams are rather oppressive.

00:08:47.444 --> 00:08:50.114
Some white enamel could
lighten it right up.

00:08:51.323 --> 00:08:54.411
- I'll do it.
- Now, you know we can't pay you.

00:08:54.578 --> 00:08:56.538
Well, everybody has to start somewhere.

00:08:56.705 --> 00:08:59.709
And the value it'll add to my portfolio
alone will be worth it.

00:08:59.876 --> 00:09:01.711
It'll be my calling card.

00:09:01.962 --> 00:09:03.839
And we should get started right away.

00:09:04.006 --> 00:09:07.010
You will have to pay for the floors,
the linens, the silverware.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.306
Unless you want patrons eating
with their hands, like Jimmy does.

00:09:10.472 --> 00:09:13.309
Happy place. Happy place. Happy place.

00:09:13.601 --> 00:09:15.187
How much, Julie?

00:09:15.771 --> 00:09:18.065
What do you think, Kirsten?
Low six?

00:09:18.316 --> 00:09:21.194
What? We don't have that money.
Are you skimming off the top?

00:09:21.444 --> 00:09:23.489
No, sweetie. That was you.

00:09:25.199 --> 00:09:27.285
My oasis is being violated.

00:09:27.452 --> 00:09:29.621
My happy place is
very unhappy right now.

00:09:29.747 --> 00:09:31.457
Now calm down, Jimbo. Just breathe.

00:09:31.666 --> 00:09:33.585
- I could pitch in.
- No. No.

00:09:33.752 --> 00:09:35.921
Please. I appreciate it, I do. But don't.

00:09:36.171 --> 00:09:38.758
I mean, separation of church and state.

00:09:38.925 --> 00:09:40.301
This is my thing.

00:09:40.468 --> 00:09:43.931
So, what are you saying?
That this is your happy place?

00:09:44.932 --> 00:09:46.225
- No.
- Caleb could help.

00:09:46.476 --> 00:09:48.103
No. This is my happy place.

00:09:48.353 --> 00:09:50.397
It's my oasis from
the rich and insufferable.

00:09:50.648 --> 00:09:53.485
It'd be a good investment for him.
And the best thing for you two.

00:09:53.651 --> 00:09:55.779
No. It would be the worst.
It would... No.

00:09:55.946 --> 00:09:59.075
- Kirsten, please back me up.
- He could be a silent partner.

00:09:59.242 --> 00:10:02.496
A silent assassin.
He would ruin everything.

00:10:02.704 --> 00:10:04.248
He'd want goulash on the menu.

00:10:04.373 --> 00:10:07.627
I don't think we have a choice.
We can't raise that kind of cash.

00:10:14.803 --> 00:10:17.807
- Hey, man. What's up?
- Nothing.

00:10:18.015 --> 00:10:20.560
So did you have sex
with Julie Cooper today?

00:10:20.727 --> 00:10:23.647
- What...? What...?
- I saw you at the motel.

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:26.860
What are you thinking, man?
Marissa's mom?

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.404
I know. I know what that
must have looked like...

00:10:29.571 --> 00:10:32.325
...or seemed like,
but it's not like that.

00:10:34.995 --> 00:10:37.998
- We've got a connection.
- Yeah, not anymore, you don't.

00:10:38.457 --> 00:10:40.543
- Lf Marissa finds out...
- She won't.

00:10:41.711 --> 00:10:44.423
Just like she didn't find out
about you in Tijuana?

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:48.679
It's a small town. People find out,
then they talk. It's only a matter of time.

00:10:49.304 --> 00:10:52.725
I've never felt this way about a girl,
a woman, before.

00:10:52.892 --> 00:10:55.604
Yeah, I don't care.
Tomorrow, Marissa's going to L.A.

00:10:55.771 --> 00:10:58.858
You, you're going to Julie's.
It's gonna end.

00:10:59.734 --> 00:11:02.738
Got it? It's gonna end.

00:11:14.628 --> 00:11:16.463
Hey, man. What are you doing?

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:18.633
Watching The Valley.
I picked it up on DVD.

00:11:18.758 --> 00:11:21.052
- Yeah? I talked to Luke.
- Would you just give me...

00:11:21.219 --> 00:11:23.222
...till the end of
the episode, please?

00:11:24.223 --> 00:11:25.767
- Is that Grady?
- Yeah.

00:11:26.017 --> 00:11:28.478
- He's kind of like you.
- What, handsome and charming?

00:11:28.687 --> 00:11:31.023
Geeky and sarcastic.

00:11:33.485 --> 00:11:35.362
Oh, God. He is like me.

00:11:35.529 --> 00:11:37.490
He is like me,
except with his own TV show.

00:11:37.698 --> 00:11:39.951
- I was kidding. He's just a character...
- No, no.

00:11:40.201 --> 00:11:42.788
He improvises all his lines.
That's totally him.

00:11:42.955 --> 00:11:44.206
And he's totally me.

00:11:44.373 --> 00:11:46.835
Except on a prime-time soap.
And, Ryan...

00:11:47.043 --> 00:11:49.254
...if you could have the real me
or the TV me...

00:11:49.505 --> 00:11:51.632
...which would you take?
You'd take the TV me.

00:11:51.799 --> 00:11:55.095
We're not going to L.A. I'm gonna
lose Summer to the real-life TV me.

00:11:55.345 --> 00:11:57.932
No. We're going to L.A.
We're taking the girls.

00:11:58.099 --> 00:12:00.268
Luke's breaking up with Julie
while we're gone.

00:12:00.518 --> 00:12:01.728
- You took care of it?
- Yeah.

00:12:01.978 --> 00:12:05.817
That's good. I told you you'd be back to
"Angst-Free Ryan" in no time.

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:08.528
I'll get it.

00:12:15.412 --> 00:12:16.830
Hey.

00:12:17.039 --> 00:12:20.293
- Can we talk?
- Sure.

00:12:20.418 --> 00:12:23.714
- So I'm not going to L.A.
- What? Why?

00:12:25.132 --> 00:12:28.553
You know how you said
sometimes time apart is the best thing?

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:33.726
Well, I think time apart might be
the best thing...

00:12:34.561 --> 00:12:36.313
...for us.
- You do?

00:12:36.563 --> 00:12:41.737
Since you showed up,
it's been pretty intense.

00:12:42.571 --> 00:12:46.200
Good and bad, but intense.

00:12:47.786 --> 00:12:51.290
And I don't know, maybe we just need
to be away from each other.

00:12:52.333 --> 00:12:54.044
Independent...

00:12:55.504 --> 00:12:56.922
...for a little while.

00:12:57.757 --> 00:13:00.885
You wanna start this
independent thing today?

00:13:02.638 --> 00:13:04.056
We both have clean slates.

00:13:04.473 --> 00:13:07.811
This is a good time for us
to be by ourselves.

00:13:10.522 --> 00:13:13.777
So you go to L.A., and I'm gonna
spend some time with my mom.

00:13:18.658 --> 00:13:20.827
See you.

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.671
So that was it?
That's your big plan you had to sleep on?

00:13:29.797 --> 00:13:32.508
- Lf I don't go, Marissa will.
- Fine. Except you're going.

00:13:32.717 --> 00:13:34.803
- Will your parents let us go?
- I'll handle it.

00:13:35.095 --> 00:13:37.097
- You're gonna lie?
- No, that was the old me.

00:13:37.264 --> 00:13:38.933
I've evolved. I'm a man of honor.

00:13:39.142 --> 00:13:41.645
So I need you to talk to them.
It's your specialty.

00:13:41.812 --> 00:13:43.522
Seems like a lot of things
are my specialty.

00:13:43.731 --> 00:13:46.234
Yeah, well, great leadership's
all about delegation.

00:13:46.401 --> 00:13:48.695
- So now I'm your employee?
- No. We're partners.

00:13:49.112 --> 00:13:51.949
- What do you do?
- I'm working on the business plan, okay?

00:13:52.074 --> 00:13:53.535
And that's gonna be awesome.

00:13:53.701 --> 00:13:56.705
I just need you to convince my parents,
convince Marissa...

00:13:56.956 --> 00:14:00.376
...and I'm gonna supervise.
God, it's so easy.

00:14:00.585 --> 00:14:02.713
I should go into business for myself.

00:14:03.881 --> 00:14:07.010
We crane up through the bushes.
That's perfect.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:11.474
I'm sorry, Ryan, is it just me, or do my
parents get better-Iooking every day?

00:14:11.766 --> 00:14:14.185
- Here we go.
- What?

00:14:15.145 --> 00:14:18.316
- What do you want, Seth?
- Can't a child just admire the beauty...

00:14:18.482 --> 00:14:22.446
...of his parents in the morning light?
You don't look a day over perfection.

00:14:22.613 --> 00:14:24.407
- Also, there's a party in Hollywood.
- No.

00:14:24.615 --> 00:14:26.200
- Why?
- I don't have to tell you why.

00:14:26.451 --> 00:14:28.912
- I'm just telling you no.
- See what you're doing here?

00:14:29.162 --> 00:14:31.040
- I do.
- I'm trying to tell you the truth...

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.334
...and establish trust here.
I could've lied.

00:14:33.585 --> 00:14:36.588
I could've easily said I was going
to Comicon or an IMAX movie.

00:14:36.755 --> 00:14:40.218
- All these devices at my fingertips.
- I knew you never went to that movie.

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:43.639
- Tag. You're tagged in.
- Yeah. Okay.

00:14:43.931 --> 00:14:46.059
It's a birthday party.
We'll be home by midnight.

00:14:46.225 --> 00:14:47.894
No drinking, drugs or fighting.

00:14:48.061 --> 00:14:51.190
- See?
- Now that we've covered the obvious...

00:14:51.399 --> 00:14:52.900
- Whose birthday?
- Grady Bridges.

00:14:53.735 --> 00:14:55.362
- Oh, the guy from The Valley?
- Yes.

00:14:55.612 --> 00:14:58.532
- I love him. He's so cute.
- Yeah, and, you guys...

00:14:58.783 --> 00:15:00.952
...he can get any girl
in the world he wants.

00:15:01.119 --> 00:15:04.415
Right now he wants Summer.
Okay? I have to go.

00:15:05.792 --> 00:15:07.544
Please. I have to go.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.095
You call when you get there,
and you're home by 11:30.

00:15:15.345 --> 00:15:18.391
Don't spend an extra minute in L.A.
The town will steal your soul.

00:15:18.641 --> 00:15:21.269
It's about to steal my girlfriend.
I'm the only thing...

00:15:21.394 --> 00:15:23.522
...standing between Summer and
a development deal. Thank you.

00:15:23.689 --> 00:15:27.277
Can you get me an autograph?
Your cell phone takes pictures, right?

00:15:27.527 --> 00:15:30.531
- Now you have to convince Marissa.
- Gonna make me do that too?

00:15:31.115 --> 00:15:33.660
We're business partners.
We serve different functions.

00:15:33.868 --> 00:15:36.705
I'm the brains, you're the brawn.
I'm in the ivory tower...

00:15:36.872 --> 00:15:39.709
...you're down there on the streets,
making it happen.

00:15:45.424 --> 00:15:48.303
- Hey.
- Call you back.

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:50.973
So when I said we needed to spend
some time apart...

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:53.393
...I meant more than a couple hours.
- I know.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:57.731
- What's that?
- Luke's puka shells. I just found them.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.484
Blast from the past, huh?

00:16:00.777 --> 00:16:02.988
Okay. Here's the thing.

00:16:03.197 --> 00:16:06.200
Not going to L.A. Because I'm not going,
that's not independent.

00:16:06.451 --> 00:16:09.621
To be really independent,
we both need to go to L.A. Independently.

00:16:09.788 --> 00:16:12.291
- But together at the same time.
- You sound like Seth.

00:16:12.458 --> 00:16:15.587
I know, it rubs off. Look, I gotta go.

00:16:15.754 --> 00:16:18.883
- Seth, unsupervised in a big city...
- Okay. No, I get that.

00:16:19.092 --> 00:16:21.720
Okay. And I don't want you
to miss out because of me.

00:16:22.888 --> 00:16:25.182
And, you know, we haven't had fun
in a long time.

00:16:25.349 --> 00:16:29.062
- This is gonna be fun.
- Usually you don't think anything's fun.

00:16:29.313 --> 00:16:32.316
- It's always me talking you into going.
- People change.

00:16:32.525 --> 00:16:34.903
And we're gonna be living
in the same town, right?

00:16:35.112 --> 00:16:38.366
You know, going to the same school.
And we're friends, yes?

00:16:38.616 --> 00:16:43.539
So, you know, we're gonna have to
do things independently.

00:16:43.789 --> 00:16:46.084
- But together.
- You're right.

00:16:49.379 --> 00:16:50.923
So you really want me to go?

00:16:52.216 --> 00:16:55.053
It's not about what I want.
It's about what you need.

00:16:57.097 --> 00:16:58.641
Okay.

00:16:59.809 --> 00:17:01.394
Maybe, a little.

00:17:02.271 --> 00:17:05.525
- All right. Let me just go get ready.
- All right. Cool.

00:17:18.541 --> 00:17:21.545
- So you need me, Sanford?
- Here we go.

00:17:21.837 --> 00:17:24.966
- Dad.
- Look, you did me a favor.

00:17:25.174 --> 00:17:27.594
- It's my turn to do one for you.
- Don't do me any favors.

00:17:27.844 --> 00:17:30.014
Let's hear him out. Okay?

00:17:30.264 --> 00:17:34.144
- Your chef. What's he done?
- Nothing, really. TV dinners mostly.

00:17:34.311 --> 00:17:35.854
He's terrible.

00:17:36.605 --> 00:17:40.109
- Look, I know when I'm not wanted.
- And yet you're always at our house.

00:17:40.318 --> 00:17:43.280
Marco was a sous chef at Aubergine.
He's fantastic.

00:17:43.614 --> 00:17:46.159
- Aubergine, that's a good spot.
- He could prepare...

00:17:46.326 --> 00:17:48.745
...some meals for you tonight.
- Good thinking.

00:17:48.996 --> 00:17:52.417
I can't, I'm busy. I'm having dinner
with the board of the philharmonic.

00:17:52.625 --> 00:17:55.629
Doesn't that include the editor in chief
of Riviera Magazine...

00:17:55.879 --> 00:17:59.050
...the owner of the Daily Pilot,
owner of the Mighty Ducks?

00:17:59.217 --> 00:18:02.220
Yeah, well, some of them used to be
Jimmy's clients, before...

00:18:02.471 --> 00:18:04.306
- Point being there, Julie?
- They're the tastemakers...

00:18:04.473 --> 00:18:07.894
...of Newport Beach. Why don't you
have Marco cook for them.

00:18:08.103 --> 00:18:09.938
You can't buy free publicity like that.

00:18:10.189 --> 00:18:13.026
If you have a restaurant,
you gotta cook for a lot of people.

00:18:13.192 --> 00:18:15.612
"If you have a restaurant,
you gotta cook for a lot of people."

00:18:15.779 --> 00:18:18.658
- That's our mission statement.
- We need the money, the press.

00:18:18.908 --> 00:18:20.785
- I know.
- Good idea, Jules.

00:18:21.036 --> 00:18:24.331
We just gutted the place.
There's dust all over. There's no furniture.

00:18:24.498 --> 00:18:28.336
We can do it at our house.
The kids are on their way to L.A.

00:18:28.503 --> 00:18:29.755
It's perfect.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:40.810
Oh, my God. We haven't moved in...
It's been forever now.

00:18:40.977 --> 00:18:43.147
How do people live like this?
How do you do it?

00:18:43.397 --> 00:18:46.693
I don't know. Times like these I wish
we had a Chitty Chitty Bang Bang.

00:18:46.818 --> 00:18:48.695
I always wish we had one.
It's a flying car.

00:18:48.946 --> 00:18:50.656
You know, my mom's
never home anymore.

00:18:50.865 --> 00:18:52.951
She's always sending Kaitlin
to my grandma's.

00:18:53.117 --> 00:18:55.662
Know what it sounds like to me,
as a child of divorce?

00:18:55.829 --> 00:18:59.083
- Think she's having an affair?
- When my mom started blowing me off...

00:18:59.292 --> 00:19:02.087
Oh, it's a flying car!

00:19:02.296 --> 00:19:03.964
No, my bad. Actually, that's a plane.

00:19:04.173 --> 00:19:07.177
- She's probably just working a lot.
- She's a professional woman.

00:19:07.427 --> 00:19:09.096
- Yeah, busy.
- Getting busy.

00:19:09.263 --> 00:19:12.266
- Who you think's gonna be there tonight?
- I hope Orlando Bloom.

00:19:12.433 --> 00:19:15.103
- Legolas is so hot.
- Right on. I'm hoping for a little...

00:19:15.312 --> 00:19:18.691
...Natalie Portman, Keira Knightley,
maybe Kate Bosworth myself...

00:19:19.442 --> 00:19:21.695
What? It's okay for you
to pine over Legolas?

00:19:21.862 --> 00:19:23.739
Yeah, he's an Elf.
He saved Middle-earth.

00:19:24.031 --> 00:19:25.867
That is a huge part of European history.

00:19:26.117 --> 00:19:28.328
Don't worry about it.
Tonight's gonna be fun.

00:19:32.333 --> 00:19:33.877
Luke better get it done.

00:19:36.338 --> 00:19:37.882
Well, see you soonishly.

00:19:38.424 --> 00:19:40.051
What about that date, Juju?

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.807
Let's just see how tonight goes, Caleb.
I want you focused.

00:19:48.478 --> 00:19:49.646
Bye.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:57.490
- Hey. We need to talk.
- Luke.

00:19:57.948 --> 00:20:00.785
- What if Caleb saw you?
- Yeah, what are you doing with him?

00:20:00.952 --> 00:20:04.081
Shouldn't he be washing his dentures?
Are you guys back together?

00:20:04.331 --> 00:20:05.958
- Don't start.
- You were just using me...

00:20:06.209 --> 00:20:08.253
...until Grandpa came back?

00:20:13.802 --> 00:20:17.097
Okay. But I don't have a lot of time.

00:20:17.223 --> 00:20:20.226
- Okay, but we'll talk after?
- Yeah, yeah, come on.

00:20:42.796 --> 00:20:45.174
- Who let that heavy-set girl in?
- That was a guy.

00:20:45.383 --> 00:20:46.551
Hey, girls, what's up?

00:20:46.718 --> 00:20:48.011
- I'm glad you made it.
- Hey.

00:20:48.178 --> 00:20:50.014
I wanna introduce you to some people.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:53.142
- Wait.
- How does that guy play high-school?

00:20:53.309 --> 00:20:54.436
Hollywood, man.

00:21:03.864 --> 00:21:07.160
I thought it was a clich Á, young
Hollywood doing coke with strippers.

00:21:07.327 --> 00:21:08.996
I didn't even think they
ate bread anymore.

00:21:09.162 --> 00:21:10.748
Can I borrow your phone?

00:21:17.006 --> 00:21:21.470
Boys, I want you to meet some people.
This is Summer, Marissa and some guy.

00:21:23.055 --> 00:21:26.601
- Are they on the show?
- No. This is Team Grady, right?

00:21:26.893 --> 00:21:31.732
This is my agent, this is my manager,
this is my lawyer, this is my publicist.

00:21:31.899 --> 00:21:34.361
And then this is my producing partner.

00:21:34.611 --> 00:21:38.491
- You have a producing partner?
- We control several properties, man.

00:21:38.658 --> 00:21:41.536
- Just got the rights to The Golden Girls.
- Oh, my God. No way!

00:21:41.787 --> 00:21:45.625
Yeah. We're gonna make it into a movie,
but we're gonna make the Golden Girls...

00:21:45.792 --> 00:21:48.211
...you know, young and hot.
- Oh.

00:21:50.798 --> 00:21:53.510
Luke, it's me. I wanted to make sure
you took care of it.

00:21:54.344 --> 00:21:56.513
Take care of it.

00:21:58.391 --> 00:21:59.642
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:21:59.934 --> 00:22:02.646
- So do you want to meet the cast?
- Not really. You?

00:22:02.813 --> 00:22:04.648
Yeah. Not really.

00:22:08.361 --> 00:22:10.489
- Excuse me.
- Well...

00:22:12.533 --> 00:22:14.953
- Oh, my God. What is with you?
- What?

00:22:15.245 --> 00:22:18.666
- Relax. All you L.A. Chicks are so lame.
- We're not from L.A.

00:22:18.833 --> 00:22:19.959
We're from Orange County.

00:22:20.251 --> 00:22:22.129
Orange County?

00:22:23.422 --> 00:22:25.842
- She said, "Ew."
- Glad we're not the ones fighting.

00:22:26.009 --> 00:22:27.969
Yeah, glad we're not
one of those couples.

00:22:29.721 --> 00:22:30.973
Or any kind of couple.

00:22:31.182 --> 00:22:33.685
- Right. It's definitely better.
- Yep.

00:22:36.146 --> 00:22:37.523
Hey there. Having fun yet?

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:40.986
- Hailey?
- Ryan?

00:22:44.573 --> 00:22:46.451
- What are you...?
- What are you...?

00:22:46.701 --> 00:22:50.164
Hailey, keep it moving.
Couples pay extra.

00:22:50.414 --> 00:22:51.749
Gotta go.

00:22:53.293 --> 00:22:55.045
- Is that...?
- Kirsten's sister, Hailey.

00:22:55.212 --> 00:22:57.464
- Does Kirsten know she's here?
- I doubt it.

00:22:57.590 --> 00:23:00.844
This is Kirsten's worst nightmare.
All she does is worry about her.

00:23:03.180 --> 00:23:05.892
I'm late. I thought
we were only gonna do it once.

00:23:06.059 --> 00:23:09.521
- Can we talk now? Because I really...
- Can't, gotta go be with the adults.

00:23:09.772 --> 00:23:11.190
I'll talk to you later.

00:23:15.487 --> 00:23:17.531
Newport used to be a glamorous town.

00:23:17.782 --> 00:23:21.328
An escape for Hollywood stars
like John Wayne, Robert Mitchum.

00:23:21.620 --> 00:23:25.750
The Lighthouse could be our chance
to bring those people back.

00:23:25.917 --> 00:23:29.213
Wait, Cal. I don't think even
The Lighthouse can bring back the Duke.

00:23:30.881 --> 00:23:33.760
What I mean is, we think
The Lighthouse is step one...

00:23:33.927 --> 00:23:36.680
...in the renaissance of Newport
for destination dining...

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:39.267
...a magnet for glitz and glamour...

00:23:39.517 --> 00:23:41.561
...and, well, cash.

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:47.527
Look, Jimmy and I view
The Lighthouse as a chance...

00:23:47.777 --> 00:23:50.406
...to restore the restaurant
to its former glory.

00:23:50.656 --> 00:23:53.243
It's just something from Newport,
for Newport.

00:23:53.493 --> 00:23:57.248
We think it can be a bit of both.
An icon of the past.

00:23:57.414 --> 00:24:01.670
- A beacon for the future.
- A bridge from the past to the present.

00:24:01.878 --> 00:24:05.508
From Newport to the rest of the world.

00:24:08.971 --> 00:24:10.556
- Hello, everybody.
- Hey, Julie.

00:24:11.265 --> 00:24:14.144
So sorry I'm late.
I hope I didn't miss anything.

00:24:14.394 --> 00:24:16.730
- Hey.
- You are glowing.

00:24:16.981 --> 00:24:20.402
Well, I'm just so excited.

00:24:32.333 --> 00:24:33.752
You have one new message.

00:24:33.918 --> 00:24:37.757
Luke, it's me. I'm just calling
to make sure you took care of it.

00:24:37.923 --> 00:24:39.592
Take care of it.

00:24:55.612 --> 00:24:57.323
Hey.

00:24:57.573 --> 00:24:58.616
Are you happy, Coop?

00:24:58.783 --> 00:25:02.204
These the kind of people we want?
Because we're gonna be stuck with them.

00:25:02.454 --> 00:25:04.665
I know, Sandy.
It's not what we wanted exactly.

00:25:05.792 --> 00:25:07.752
It's exactly not what we wanted at all.

00:25:07.919 --> 00:25:10.923
Look, we need the money.
Without Caleb, we've got nothing.

00:25:11.090 --> 00:25:12.341
Maybe nothing is better.

00:25:12.550 --> 00:25:16.263
That's an easy position to take if you
have another job. This is all I have.

00:25:16.513 --> 00:25:18.808
- Hello?
- Sandy, hey, it's me.

00:25:19.058 --> 00:25:22.354
- Ryan? Is everything okay?
- Not really.

00:25:22.563 --> 00:25:25.483
- We found Hailey.
- What do you mean, you found Hailey?

00:25:25.691 --> 00:25:27.944
- Hailey?
- Well, she got a job...

00:25:28.111 --> 00:25:29.696
...as a stripper.

00:25:30.990 --> 00:25:33.910
- There are strippers at this party?
- Strippers?

00:25:34.119 --> 00:25:35.704
I never should've agreed to this.

00:25:35.954 --> 00:25:38.666
- What do you want us to do?
- There's nothing you can do.

00:25:38.916 --> 00:25:42.671
- Hailey is not your responsibility.
- Where are they? Is she okay?

00:25:42.838 --> 00:25:46.134
- What club are you at?
- It's Luna Chicks.

00:25:46.384 --> 00:25:50.306
Luna Chicks? Well, that's just great.

00:25:51.098 --> 00:25:53.977
- What are you gonna do?
- I will deal with Hailey tomorrow.

00:25:54.269 --> 00:25:56.855
Meanwhile, I want you guys home.
Pronto.

00:25:57.106 --> 00:25:58.691
All right.

00:26:00.151 --> 00:26:02.237
- What's going on?
- They found Hailey.

00:26:02.404 --> 00:26:05.283
- Working as a stripper at this party.
- Is she okay?

00:26:05.533 --> 00:26:07.160
No, of course not, no.
She's Hailey.

00:26:07.410 --> 00:26:08.620
Should we do something?

00:26:09.162 --> 00:26:11.999
You know what? We should not let
Hailey ruin another evening.

00:26:12.291 --> 00:26:15.879
We got enough to contend with,
and if Kirsten finds out about this...

00:26:16.129 --> 00:26:18.257
- I don't know...
- We'll deal with it tomorrow.

00:26:18.424 --> 00:26:22.054
- Everything is going so well.
- Everyone seems really excited.

00:26:22.179 --> 00:26:24.890
What the hell is that smell?

00:26:25.767 --> 00:26:29.021
- What are we cooking here?
- Meat loaf. It's my mother's specialty.

00:26:29.187 --> 00:26:31.857
I have the most important people
in the county in there...

00:26:32.066 --> 00:26:33.735
...the most sophisticated palates
in Newport...

00:26:33.902 --> 00:26:36.029
...and you offer them Nana Cohen's
meat loaf?

00:26:36.238 --> 00:26:38.491
- Dad. It's their menu.
- The menu of lunatics.

00:26:38.741 --> 00:26:41.912
This is a disaster. I'll have to
call Catherine Zeta-Jones' people.

00:26:42.079 --> 00:26:44.039
I was trying to get her for the opening.

00:26:44.206 --> 00:26:47.168
How quickly can you get to the
Crab Shack and pick up some fresh tuna?

00:26:47.335 --> 00:26:49.755
Whoa. No, Marco. This is our restaurant.

00:26:49.922 --> 00:26:53.593
You don't have a restaurant without me
and you don't have me with meat loaf.

00:26:53.802 --> 00:26:55.387
Well, then, maybe we're better off.

00:26:55.637 --> 00:26:58.057
A man's life comes down to
a few decisive moments...

00:26:58.265 --> 00:27:02.062
...and maybe this meat loaf
is one of them.

00:27:02.229 --> 00:27:04.941
This restaurant was supposed to be fun.

00:27:05.107 --> 00:27:08.278
If you wanna go and ruin everything
that this restaurant is about...

00:27:08.528 --> 00:27:11.574
...then go ahead. Fine.
I don't want any part of it.

00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:14.953
Good night. Good luck.

00:27:19.375 --> 00:27:21.795
That's why the man is bankrupt.

00:27:21.962 --> 00:27:24.131
Do what you like. Sink the ship.

00:27:24.298 --> 00:27:25.967
But make it quick. I'm starving.

00:27:26.551 --> 00:27:30.431
Hey, Marco, there's a lot
riding on this meat loaf.

00:27:34.144 --> 00:27:36.438
- Julie, is that a...?
- Curling-iron burn.

00:27:36.689 --> 00:27:38.274
Yeah.

00:27:38.524 --> 00:27:40.276
I'm gonna go check on Cal.

00:27:41.737 --> 00:27:44.740
- This place is too crowded.
- Soon as we find Seth and Summer...

00:27:44.991 --> 00:27:46.910
...we're out of here.
- And Hailey.

00:27:47.160 --> 00:27:51.332
- I don't know. It's none of my business.
- Yeah, it is. It's your family.

00:27:52.166 --> 00:27:55.045
We need to find her and get out of here.

00:27:56.630 --> 00:27:59.842
All right, you wait here.
If you see Seth, don't let him move.

00:28:00.051 --> 00:28:02.846
- And I'll just go try to find her.
- Not without me.

00:28:04.473 --> 00:28:05.641
Come on.

00:28:06.726 --> 00:28:10.898
Cheers, cheers.
To me, in all my glory...

00:28:11.065 --> 00:28:12.900
...and a second season.

00:28:18.449 --> 00:28:23.497
- Hey.
- Hi. Hi. How's it going?

00:28:23.747 --> 00:28:25.750
- I'm so exhausted.
- Yeah?

00:28:25.958 --> 00:28:28.211
I've been up all night working
on my thesis.

00:28:28.378 --> 00:28:30.506
"Magical Realism in
American Literature."

00:28:30.756 --> 00:28:32.675
Familiar with the works of
Thomas Pynchon?

00:28:33.343 --> 00:28:39.225
- I've only read The Crying of Lot 49.
- Gravity's Rainbow is his masterpiece.

00:28:42.104 --> 00:28:45.066
- Don't tell anyone I'm in grad school.
- Okay.

00:28:45.274 --> 00:28:49.071
So I've got a new episode that
hasn't aired yet. You wanna see it?

00:28:49.279 --> 00:28:52.658
- No way. You have a new episode?
- Yeah, on tape. Yeah?

00:28:52.909 --> 00:28:55.245
Yeah. Hold on, I just have to...

00:28:55.495 --> 00:28:59.542
Oh, yeah, no.
I'm not armed or anything.

00:29:04.674 --> 00:29:06.718
- Yeah, that's a...
- Camera phone.

00:29:06.926 --> 00:29:08.804
It's the autograph of the 21 st century.

00:29:08.971 --> 00:29:11.140
Yeah. That's what they say.
That's what they say.

00:29:12.976 --> 00:29:14.269
Let's go.

00:29:14.436 --> 00:29:16.146
Call me sometime.

00:29:16.814 --> 00:29:18.274
I will.

00:29:27.744 --> 00:29:28.996
There you are.

00:29:29.288 --> 00:29:33.418
- I thought you'd flown the coop as well.
- Just trying to get a little peace and quiet.

00:29:33.585 --> 00:29:36.046
Wax philosophical about why
your partner up and quit.

00:29:36.296 --> 00:29:38.758
He hasn't quit.
He went after Hailey.

00:29:38.966 --> 00:29:41.261
What are you talking about?
Hailey's in Club Med.

00:29:41.470 --> 00:29:44.765
Oh, she's in a club, but in Hollywood,
working as a stripper.

00:29:45.016 --> 00:29:47.727
Ryan just called. They found her.

00:29:48.270 --> 00:29:51.315
Anyway, that's where my partner went.

00:29:52.900 --> 00:29:54.653
And that's why he's my partner.

00:30:06.209 --> 00:30:11.048
This is so cool. You're here, and here.
It's awesome.

00:30:11.215 --> 00:30:14.928
- I'm out of here. "La-tro."
- Oh, my God. I bet that was improvised.

00:30:16.930 --> 00:30:20.602
- Listen, I'm really glad that you came...
- No, wait. I wanna watch.

00:30:22.229 --> 00:30:24.648
Why? I'm not in this scene.

00:30:24.815 --> 00:30:27.068
It's just so good.

00:30:28.361 --> 00:30:29.780
I wish I was from the Valley.

00:30:35.954 --> 00:30:39.292
- Hey, where's Summer?
- I don't know, off with Grady somewhere.

00:30:39.500 --> 00:30:42.254
I talk about Pynchon for two seconds,
suddenly she's gone.

00:30:42.421 --> 00:30:44.089
- I got something else for you.
- Dude.

00:30:45.550 --> 00:30:48.011
You have a clean slate now,
so if I was you...

00:30:48.261 --> 00:30:50.848
...I'd procure a little
private dance time with...

00:30:59.859 --> 00:31:02.279
- Oh, my God. That's Hailey.
- Yeah. That's what l...

00:31:04.991 --> 00:31:06.993
Hey, hey, what the hell are you doing?

00:31:07.160 --> 00:31:10.664
I thought you were an aerobics instructor
in the Caribbean or something.

00:31:10.873 --> 00:31:12.834
I figured the truth wouldn't
go over so well.

00:31:13.001 --> 00:31:14.669
My mom will freak
when she finds out.

00:31:14.878 --> 00:31:16.422
Don't tell her.
Not that she'd care.

00:31:16.588 --> 00:31:17.882
She would if she knew
what you're doing.

00:31:18.132 --> 00:31:20.760
What's wrong with it?
I make good money, I'm on my own.

00:31:21.011 --> 00:31:22.763
You look terrible.
You work here?

00:31:23.013 --> 00:31:25.475
Let me just grab my girlfriend,
and we'll go figure it out.

00:31:25.641 --> 00:31:27.852
What, tired today?
Didn't do enough coke?

00:31:28.061 --> 00:31:29.313
Hey, take it easy, man.

00:31:29.563 --> 00:31:31.983
- Get back to work.
- Don't tell her what to do.

00:31:32.442 --> 00:31:34.736
- Excuse me? You got a problem?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:31:35.028 --> 00:31:36.488
- I do.
- No, he doesn't. I'm sorry.

00:31:36.739 --> 00:31:39.075
We're gonna grab my girlfriend
and grab my aunt...

00:31:39.325 --> 00:31:42.204
...more gently than you, and we'll leave.
- You're leaving now.

00:31:42.454 --> 00:31:45.625
Get them out of my club.
Out, out, out.

00:31:47.210 --> 00:31:51.465
Bye. Nice meeting you.
I don't wanna see them in my club again.

00:32:02.396 --> 00:32:05.691
- Are we gonna just leave Hailey here?
- I don't think we have a choice.

00:32:05.942 --> 00:32:09.238
- We can't leave without her.
- I can't get ahold of Summer.

00:32:09.488 --> 00:32:11.657
I think we should split up.
Let's scale a wall.

00:32:11.782 --> 00:32:14.369
Find a fire escape.
Climb through a window. The usual.

00:32:15.913 --> 00:32:19.250
I was all-camp "Capture the Flag,"
Camp Tuckahoe. I'm very stealth.

00:32:24.215 --> 00:32:26.843
That's kind of dewy.
I'm gonna go around.

00:32:31.974 --> 00:32:35.270
- We're going to the VIP entrance.
- We're not VIP.

00:32:35.562 --> 00:32:37.356
This is Hollywood.

00:32:37.439 --> 00:32:39.567
Meet me in a minute. I have an idea.

00:32:40.235 --> 00:32:41.820
This meat loaf is fantastic.

00:32:41.987 --> 00:32:44.407
This is what we had planned.

00:32:44.699 --> 00:32:46.409
Back to basics. Comfort food.

00:32:46.868 --> 00:32:47.994
What's old is new again.

00:32:48.245 --> 00:32:50.164
I couldn't have said that better myself.

00:32:50.414 --> 00:32:53.293
- Even though I already did.
- So glad that you like it.

00:32:53.543 --> 00:32:55.879
- I'm going to get more wine. Anyone?
- Oh, terrific.

00:33:33.927 --> 00:33:35.470
Juju.

00:33:35.679 --> 00:33:36.889
Bring the wine, dear.

00:33:38.808 --> 00:33:40.894
This one's empty.
I'm gonna get another.

00:33:49.822 --> 00:33:51.490
What the hell are you doing here?

00:33:51.699 --> 00:33:53.660
